I prefer to play with tiles. (nethackW). I find it much much easier to
see what's going on with tiles rather than ascii, and it's not just
about knowing which letter is what =96 it's a matter of clarity of
information. With tiles I can see the difference between a mind flayer
and a dwarf very clearly, with ascii I sometimes get it wrong, and the
results are fatal. I find it easier to remember which picture is which
monster, as opposed to remembering which letter and colour corresponds
to each monster - and which colours are shared. I sure like being able
to see what kind of weapon or armour is on the ground without using ;
to find out what the [ represents. To me, the ascii graphics are a
cute idea, a fun tradition, a useful tool for enabling online play -
but ultimate an inferior way to play the game. Some people say they
find it easier to see what's going on with ascii rather than the
pictures. I don't really understand why, but all I can really say is
all the more power to them. They apparently have an advantage over me
on NAO. ;)


